From ae8290efe5bab0f18e22d48505f2b6fc6f79ddb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 17:59:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webui: Settings tab field fixes from a four-radio tester

Numeric boxes are as wide as the selects: the unit (dBm, s) sits inside the
box instead of beside it, so the Roaming assistant threshold and Group Key
Rotation align with the rows around them.

A shared nvram key shown in two columns (the DFS and U-NII-4 options on a
box with two 5 GHz radios) is mirrored on change, counted once and posted
once from an unlocked copy. Before, each copy counted and the last copy in
the page won at apply, so a tick under 5 GHz-1 was silently dropped by the
untouched box under 5 GHz-2. The row's help now says what the boxes are and
that a fixed DFS channel still moves when radar is detected (RWFP_49, all
packs).

Extension Channel offers only the sidebands the driver lists for the chosen
channel: 13 is Below only, 1 is Above only. The composer already corrected
an impossible pick on apply; the page showed the other one.

Fragmentation Threshold stays editable in Legacy mode only, as on the stock
page; its help says so (new RWFP_83, translated in 25 packs) in addition to
the hover reason.

Set AP Isolated leaves the page: on this build isolation is a per-network
setting on the Network menu, and the per-radio key here reached only the
primary BSS. wlpro_nv_fields loses ap_isolate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
